## Observability

OpenTelemetry traces and metrics are wired in from day one. The service name comes from
`OTEL_SERVICE_NAME` (default: the repository slug; under `mise` an inherited value is ignored —
set it in `mise.local.toml`); browser bundles cannot read the environment, so vite/sveltekit use
build-time `VITE_OTEL_SERVICE_NAME` and Angular uses `environment.serviceName`.

Run `mise run otel` to start the shared system-wide Collector + Aspire Dashboard stack (Docker
required). `mise` then sets `OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_ENDPOINT` and the per-signal endpoint variables
automatically. Open `http://127.0.0.1:18888` and use Aspire's Traces, Metrics, and Structured Logs
pages to inspect received telemetry. Viewer data is memory-only and resets when the dashboard
container restarts.

Use `mise run otel:status` to check Collector health and viewer reachability separately,
`mise run otel:logs` to tail the raw Collector output, and `mise run otel:down` to stop the whole
stack. Retained raw data also lands as newline-delimited JSON in the `forge-otel-data` Docker
volume (`/data/traces.jsonl`, `metrics.jsonl`, and `logs.jsonl`). The Structured Logs page contains
only logs an application exports over OTLP; its presence does not mean every stack has an
application log bridge.

Browser bundles cannot read the environment, so the endpoint is inlined at build time. Vite and
SvelteKit read `VITE_OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_ENDPOINT`. Angular uses `mise run dev` / `mise run build`
(fullstack: `mise run web-dev` / `mise run web-build`), which pass `OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_ENDPOINT`
to `ng` via `--define`; plain `npm start` / `ng build` stays silent by design. Those Angular tasks
refuse an endpoint containing `"`, `\` or control characters.

To point at a different collector, set `OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_ENDPOINT` (and the per-signal and
`VITE_` variables you use) under `[env]` in `mise.local.toml`. Under `mise`, `mise.local.toml`
wins over `.config/mise/conf.d/otel.toml`, which wins over your shell, so an `export` in the
shell is ignored for tasks `mise` runs.

Outside `mise` (for example a bare `go run`, an IDE run configuration, or a CI job that does not
shell through `mise`), nothing is exported unless you set `OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_ENDPOINT` yourself
(Vite and SvelteKit: `VITE_OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_ENDPOINT`; Angular exports only through its `mise`
tasks).
